From 4444444444444444444444444444444444444444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: camera: add the downstream msm-camera header

qcs6490-camera.dtsi, the CAMX (Spectra) camera description, uses the CPAS
path and transaction constants from <dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h>.
Mainline carries no such header: CPAS is the downstream camera bus
arbiter, and mainline CAMSS votes bandwidth through the generic
interconnect bindings instead, so it needs none of these definitions.

Add the header verbatim from the Qualcomm downstream kernel so the CAMX
overlay compiles. It previously reached the kernel tree through the
recipe's files/ overlay, which is copied over ${S} outside do_patch and
so is invisible to the patch series.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream Qualcomm binding]
Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
---
 include/dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h | 155 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 155 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h

diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h b/include/dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..97228c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/camera/msm-camera.h
@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
